{"engine_version":"0.37.0","file":"leo-pvt-fjord-skyline.toml","toml":"# Fused MEO and LEO positioning for a vessel deep in a fjord, where the valley walls hide\n# everything low across the channel: the `leo-pvt` joint mode under the `fjord` skyline\n# preset.\n#\n# The question a coastal-navigation or ferry operator asks: the walls of a deep fjord leave\n# a strip of sky along the channel, so how much does a low Earth orbit (LEO) layer add to GPS\n# and Galileo there, where the passes are short and fast? The fjord runs north-south with\n# walls rising to 600 m above the antenna 1.5 km either side: 21.8 deg across the channel,\n# below 1 deg along it, each wall point lowered by the Earth's curvature (4/3 effective\n# radius). The site is a generic point in western Norway at 61.1 N, 6.6 E; the systems are\n# those of `meo-leo-fused-pvt.toml` (GPS baseline, Galileo, the public Xona Pulsar X5\n# signal), each with its own receiver clock, and the same skyline applies over each system's\n# own elevation mask. Each epoch reports `masked_by_skyline`.\n#\n# The skyline preset is REPRESENTATIVE (provenance in docs/SKYLINE.md and `kshana skyline\n# --preset fjord`): the order of the width and relief of the deep west-Norwegian fjords, not\n# a survey of any fjord. Line of sight only: no diffraction, reflection or non-line-of-sight\n# reception. Remove the [skyline] section to compare with open sky. MODELLED.\nkind = \"leo-pvt\"\nmode = \"joint\"\nseed = 3\nduration_s = 1800.0\nstep_s = 30.0\n\n[user]\nlat_deg = 61.1\nlon_deg = 6.6\nheight_m = 20.0\n\n[joint]\nmax_leo_sweep = 12\n\n[[system]]\nname = \"GPS\"\npreset = \"gps-baseline\"\ncn0_dbhz = [38.0, 48.0]\nsisre_m = 0.6\n\n[[system]]\nname = \"Galileo\"\npreset = \"galileo\"\ncn0_dbhz = [38.0, 48.0]\nsisre_m = 0.3\nisb_ns = 12.0\n\n[[system]]\nname = \"Pulsar X5\"\nleo_preset = \"xona-pulsar\"\nsignal = \"X5\"\nisb_ns = 40.0\n\n[skyline]\npreset = \"fjord\"\n","summary":"LEO PVT (joint) at 61.10, 6.60 over 1800 s\n  GPS          gnss    24 sats at  20182 km, 1575.42 MHz\n  Galileo      gnss    24 sats at  23222 km, 1575.42 MHz\n  Pulsar X5    leo    258 sats at   1080 km, 1190.52 MHz\n  LEO ranging satellite in view on 100.0% of epochs\n  GNSS only  availability 1.000, median PDOP 1.48, RMS 3D error 1.29 m\n  LEO only   availability 1.000, median PDOP 2.33, RMS 3D error 0.69 m\n  fused      availability 1.000, median PDOP 1.14, RMS 3D error 0.63 m\n","json":"{\n  \"doppler\": null,\n  \"duration_s\": 1800.0,\n  \"joint\": {\n    \"dop_sweep\": [\n      {\n        \"median_hdop\": 0.7263605574121064,\n        \"median_pdop\": 1.476359784256664,\n        \"median_vdop\": 1.2820533305247284,\n        \"n_epochs\": 61,\n        \"n_leo\": 0\n      },\n      {\n        \"median_hdop\": 0.7263605574121065,\n        \"median_pdop\": 1.476359784256662,\n        \"median_vdop\": 1.282053330524729,\n        \"n_epochs\": 61,\n        \"n_leo\": 1\n      },\n      {\n        \"median_hdop\": 0.7047218000813368,\n        \"median_pdop\": 1.415989675657616,\n        \"median_vdop\": 1.2355245664774257,\n        \"n_epochs\": 61,\n        \"n_leo\": 2\n      },\n      {\n        \"median_hdop\": 0.6799269125446997,\n        \"median_pdop\": 1.3951141496704336,\n        \"median_vdop\": 1.213663124142023,\n        \"n_epochs\": 61,\n        \"n_leo\": 3\n      },\n      {\n        \"median_hdop\": 0.6618537528998908,\n        \"median_pdop\": 1.369319818900099,\n        \"median_vdop\": 1.201712498660821,\n        \"n_epochs\": 61,\n        \"n_leo\": 4\n      },\n      {\n        \"median_hdop\": 0.6296903430381451,\n        \"median_pdop\": 1.3252725121041729,\n        \"median_vdop\": 1.1671994165614399,\n        \"n_epochs\": 61,\n        \"n_leo\": 5\n      },\n      {\n        \"median_hdop\": 0.6076227930525754,\n        \"median_pdop\": 1.294164133125572,\n        \"median_vdop\": 1.1401263323842348,\n        \"n_epochs\": 61,\n        \"n_leo\": 6\n      },\n      {\n        \"median_hdop\"